(defn- acc-code [] :string "~nGit^;uf'0nGrW>;uf&Eq*:J>q*4umd/X:]lOX+^;uf$Iq*:VBM\\-R5WB`c^nJMBM;uf\"Td/a.WlOX&';uf!HWOl+#W<$5rW<-T(W<6r3W<@;>q*5)Hq*:bEM\\-EedXVN5dXY.'Rh.D1M\\$?`dsUL6OUV>mnGit^dX[8cRZ%9K&-+-hq*Y8Jq*YDOq*Y\\Qq*YhVq*Z7cnGrW>;ue0dWWWFqWW`LsWWiRuWX/e$WX8k&dXV?8dn`)o[/^6HZiDB:nH8kW;ue2<ph>$CnH8b4;ue1/d/X>BP!C$[OT5P6P!C$:WXo/`dXV?%OT7$Od/X<GP!C\"`dsj?1OTGQ1d\\$R;dXV<9pj.:(lO<q\\qHVFD;ud#/dn`)gZiC,<d/X<Gdsj?1dsjG>WY#=nOT5VinGkp`<<)rKdXV<%OTEWB'EA+PZiD5+nH8kW;ue%-ph>$CnH8b4;ue#ud/X>BP!C$[OT5P6P!C$:WXo/`dXV?%OT7$O(]XO\"M]*%Dq*9N@q*4unb7Oh2M\\,ulP!C%iM[]]Hphb<=P!C#,M]**Cb8LI\"OT5b+P!BH1dmX,hZiCW+M];_BnGrSR;udo>WWWG#WZ)'<OT6=;nGje`;ud%QWW`LlnGiU)RZ5e`nGkki;ucnmdXVB.R`ut.P!D-_ZiD$0nH8kW;udi2ph>$CnH8b4;udh%d/X>BP!C$[OT5P6P!C$:WXo/`dXV?1b67r%nGiVTRZZ(hnGkm?;ucnmdXVB2RaE72P!D-_P'A'PW^J(8d/YD=OT70SlPoo>;ud%nWW`LpnGiVTRZZ(hnGkm?;ucnmdXVB2RaE72P!D-_ZiClAnH8kW;ud\\Cph>$CnH8b4;ud[6d/X>BP!C$[OT5P6P!C$:WXo/`b68!1nGiVTRZZ(hnGkm?;ucnmdXVB2RaE72P!D-_b68!1dXV?-b7OcOP!C\"`OT6mK'EA+@b8^MYP!C\"`WZ2-2nGiVTRZZ(hnGkm?;ucnmdXVB2RaE72P!D-_dXVB.b8UJaRa!3Lb6%i/d/XDgdXV<PRa!$2lOa-S;ucq+P<_7TOT5QedXV<PRbK#@b7OcWP<_:5'EA+7P<_7TM\\uLkpi(NJRh1\"MP<_:5OT6%3M];s=OT5UtlOX(=;udFRb8:6cO['BFlPT\\P;ucompg\\Tspb@(:OT5Mo(]XO4pj%/4pb@((OT5V2(]XLtnGkeG;uct#OT7XlnGr_V;ud@9OT::VOT5UtlOX(=;ud>Zb8:6cO['BFpg\\Tspb@(:OT5MolPT\\P<<)uN(]XLcdXVT7b6%eWOT5b+M\\$+1lPKXE;ud9Cb8:6cO['BF&-)]MMZX;@'EA+9nGiS3;ucu-d/X=Uq#g`_q#gldq#h/fq#h;kq#h`#q#CQ]WBjb]WBt+hWC(IsWC1h)W5V^,emANpWY5KqWY>QsWYGWuWYP^$WYYd&q#g`_q#gldq#h/fq#h;kq#h`#q#CQ]WBjb]WBt+hWC(IsWC1h)W5V^,'EA,a")
;; zag's tree start when every value of 0..63 is in 0..63, else 0
(defn- acc-zag [M :vector-i64 zg :i64] :i64
 (let [t (qb-tree M zg)]
  (if (and (> t 0) (loop [x 0] (or (= x 64) (let [z (gn-tree-value M t x)] (and (>= z 0) (<= z 63) (recur (inc x))))))) t 0)))
(defn- acc-admit [M :vector-i64 i :i64] :bool
 (let [p (dec i) f (gn-sir M p IF-A)]
  (and (> p 0) (< (+ p 154) (vector-at M MM-SIR-N)) (= (gn-op M p) OP-FN) (> f 0) (< f (vector-at M MM-FN-N))
   (= (gn-fnf M f FF-SIR) p) (= (gn-fnf M f FF-NPARAMS) 4) (= (gn-fnf M f FF-PT0) TY-VEC)
   (= (gn-fnf M f (+ FF-PT0 1)) TY-I64) (= (gn-fnf M f (+ FF-PT0 2)) TY-I64) (= (gn-fnf M f (+ FF-PT0 3)) TY-I64)
   (= (gn-fnf M f FF-RTYPE) TY-VEC)
   (let [hs (gn-sir M (+ p 12) IF-A) bs (gn-sir M (+ p 36) IF-A) fl (gn-sir M (+ p 64) IF-A) zc (gn-sir M (+ p 74) IF-A)
         ex (gn-sir M (+ p 78) IF-A) zg (gn-sir M (+ p 83) IF-A) s16 (gn-sir M (+ p 92) IF-A) pt (gn-sir M (+ p 93) IF-A)
         hq (kfn-q M hs) bt (if (> hq 0) (gn-sir M (+ hq 4) IF-A) 0) hc (if (> hq 0) (gn-sir M (+ hq 12) IF-A) 0)
         eq (kfn-q M ex) pw (if (> eq 0) (gn-sir M (+ eq 15) IF-A) 0)]
    (and (> hq 0) (> eq 0) (not= hs f) (not= bs f) (not= zc f) (not= ex f) (> (acc-zag M zg) 0)
     (pj-fn? M f 154 (acc-pat) [f hs bs fl zc ex zg s16 pt]) (pj-fn? M hs 15 (acs-pat) [hs bt hc])
     (pj-fn? M zc 29 (acz-pat) [zc zg pt]) (pj-fn? M ex 36 (ace-pat) [ex pw s16])
     (pj-fn? M s16 19 (pj-i16-pat) [s16 65535 32768 65536])
     (> (kfn-q M hc) 0) (> (kfn-q M bs) 0)
     (hfc-admit M (inc (kfn-q M hc))) (hbt-admit M (inc (kfn-q M bs)))
     (= (gn-sir M (+ (kfn-q M hc) 67) IF-A) bt) (= (gn-sir M (+ (kfn-q M bs) 86) IF-A) pw)
     (= (gn-sir M (+ (kfn-q M bs) 99) IF-A) pt))))))
;; the end of block's run: word 265 + j of the block is str xzr, [x16, #8 zag(j)]
(defn- acc-zst [M :vector-i64 t :i64 at :i64 k :i64] :vector-i64
 (if (= k 64) M
  (acc-zst (gn-put M (+ MM-CODE-BASE (+ at k)) (enc-str 31 16 (* 8 (gn-tree-value M t k)))) t at (inc k))))
(defn- acc-entry [M :vector-i64 i :i64] :vector-i64
 (if (not (acc-admit M i)) M
  (let [p (dec i) t (acc-zag M (gn-sir M (+ p 83) IF-A)) at (+ (vector-at M MM-CODE-N) 265)]
   (gn-tree-data (acc-zst (kemit-hex M (acc-code)) t at 0) t 0 64))))

;; ---- picojpeg coefficient-block: (f v block) reads the block's component, quant (512 / 576) and DC table, puts the
;; block into v[1610], decodes the DC difference (huff-symbol, bits(width, 1), extend(r, symbol)), stores i16(dc) into
;; v[1510 + component] and i16(dc * v[quant]) into v[1536], then tail-calls ac-coefficients(v, 2 / 3, quant, 1).
;; Before the frame, with block and component 0..15 and v live past item 1610, the DC part is computed in registers
;; (the reader's cells, huff-symbol and bits as in ac-coefficients' block), its charges summed (1, put8 2, huff-symbol,
;; bits, extend 1, two puts) and checked; only then are v[1610], the DC cells and the reader's cells stored and the
;; counter published, and the kernel branches to ac-coefficients with the arguments set (x30 untouched: a tail call).
;; Anything else (a refill from the input, offset >= 256, the marker byte, fuel short) leaves the call untouched to
;; coefficient-block's own code. Generated and checked against the source semantics outside the compiler. The T2 keep
;; marker ends the block (only the way into coefficient-block's own code passes it), so T2 keeps the kernel without
;; relying on a rollback.
(defn- cbk-pat [] :string "~!!3,n!!3-0!\"o83!!!!!!\"&Q=!!!!!!!E9%!!*'\"!!<3%\"k!AN!!E9'!!3-#!!WE(!!*'\"!\"K\"5!!!!#!!N?)!!!!!!!<3$!WW3#!!E9&!!*'\"!!<3&\"f_P&!!E9(!!<3$!!WE(!!3-#!\"K\"5!!*'$!!<3&!!!!!!!`K)!!*'\"!\"/c-qud!\"!!<3%!!!!!!\"/W*!!!!!!\"&Q+!!!!!!!<3%!'gMa!\"&Q)!!!!!!!WE(!!!!!!!N?*!!!!!!!E9%!!*'\"!!<3%\"hjs:!!E9'!!<3$!!WE(!!*'\"!\"K\"5!!!!#!!<3%!!!!!!!`K)!!!!!!\"/c,qt0ph!!<3$!!!!!!\"/Vp!!!!!!\"&Pq!!!!!!!<3$!!*'\"!\"&Po!!!!!!!N?+!!!!!!!E9%!!*'\"!!<3%#\"ejq!!E9'!!3-#!\"Ju$!!!!$!!E9&!!N?&!\"Ju#!!!!#!!N?,!!!!!!!E9%!!WE'!!<3%!=&T)!\"K\"5!!!!#!!N?-!!!!!!!E9%!!`K(!!<3%!\"T&0!!WE,!!!!!!!N?.!!!!!!!E9%!!iQ)!!<3%!!!!!!!`K)!!!!!!\"/c,qqM/O!!E9%!!WE'!\"/VT!!!!!!\"&PX!!!!!!!E9%!!WE'!!E9&!!iQ)!!<3&!!*'\"!\"Ju\"!!!!$!\"&PS!!!!!!!N?/!!!!!!!E9%!!iQ)!!<3%!!!!!!!`K)!!!!!!\"/c,qp,6B!!<3$!!!!!!\"/VH!!!!!!\"&PK!!!!!!!E9%!!rW*!!<3%!=&T)!\"K\"5!!!!#!\"&PG!!!!!!!N?0!!!!!!!E9%!\"&]+!!E9&!!`K(!\"Ju!!!!!#!!E9&!!rW*!!<3&\"m,db!!E9(!!<3$!!WE(!!3-#!\"K\"5!!*'$!!WE(!!!!!!!<3%s6]je!!WE,!!!!!!!N?1!!!!!!!E9%!!rW*!!<3%\"m,db!!E9'!!<3$!!WE(!!*'\"!!E9'!\"/c,!\"Jtu!!3-$!\"Jtt!!!!$!!<3%\"onW'!!E9'!\"/c,!!E9(!!rW*!!E9)!!E9%!\"K\"5!!<3&!!WE*!!3-#!\"Jtu!!3-$!\"Jtt!!!!$!!N?2!!!!!!!E9%!\"8i-!!<3%\"ipZD!!E9'!!<3$!!WE(!!*'\"!\"K\"5!!!!#!!<3%!!!!!!!`K)!!!!!!\"/c,qkF,k!!<3$!!3-#!\"/Us!!!!!!\"&Ot!!!!!!!<3$!!<3$!\"&Or!!!!!!!N?3!!!!!!!E9%!\"8i-!!E9&!\"Ao.!!E9'!!E9%!!<3'!!*'\"!\"Jts!!!!%!##>4!!!!!!!<2o!!!!!")
(defn- cbk-code-a [] :string "~nGk[9;ue!Gq*:J>q*4umd/X:]lOX+^;udtKq*:VBM\\-R5WB`c^nJNr$;udrVq*:bEM\\-EeMZF:Vq,^/inGk[Y;udpEWOl+#W<$5rW<-T(W<6r3W<@;>MZO@Zq,XM7dXXRbZiC)&dXXjjq,[?2nGiV4R\\'iPdXVN5dXY.+Rh/#mM\\$?`dsUPfOUV@Cq*Y8Jq*YDOq*Y\\Qq*YhVq*Z7cq*5)HdXV@Cdn`)o[/^6HZiCrcnH8kW;udbeph>$CnH8b4;udaXd/X>BP!C$[OT5P6P!C$:WXo/`dXV?%OT7$Od/X<GP!C\"`dsj?1OTGQ1d\\$R;dXV<9pj.:(lO<q\\qHVFD;ud#/dn`)gZiC,<d/X<Gdsj?1dsjG>WY#=nOT5VinGkp`<<)rKdXV<%OTEWB'EA+PZiCeTnH8kW;udUVph>$CnH8b4;udTId/X>BP!C$[OT5P6P!C$:WXo/`dXV?%OT7$O(]XO\"M]*%Dq*9N@q*4unb7Oh2M\\,ulP!C%iM[]]Hphb<=P!C#,M]**Cb8LI\"OT5b+WWiS$P!BH1ZiCIQWWWG#WZ)'<OT6=;nGje`;ud%QWW`LlnGiU)RZ5e`nGkki;ucnmdXVB.R`ut.P!D-_ZiCUdnH8kW;udEfph>$CnH8b4;udDYd/X>BP!C$[OT5P6P!C$:WXo/`dXV?1b67r%nGiVTRZZ(hnGkm?;ucnmdXVB2RaE72P!D-_P'A'PW^J(8d/YD=OT70SlPoo>;ud%nWW`LpnGiVTRZZ(hnGkm?;ucnmdXVB2RaE72P!D-_ZiCHunH8kW;ud9\"ph>$CnH8b4;ud7jd/X>BP!C$[OT5P6P!C$:WXo/`b68!1nGiVTRZZ(hnGkm?;ucnmdXVB2RaE72P!D-_b68!1dXV?-b7OcOP!C\"`OT6mK'EA+@b8^MYP!C\"`WZ2-2nGiVTRZZ(hnGkm?;ucnmdXVB2RaE72P!D-_dXVB.b8UJaRa!3LWWiS%'EA+7dXV<9P<_?,d/XD*nGkTl;ucqidXV<PRa<65lOa5+;ucp@OT5QedXV<PRb8l>b7OcWP<_:5q,a#(M\\#okP!D14pg\\U=Rh1\"PP<_;CP<_:5OT5n/lPKXE;ud\"&b8:6cP!C!Aq&(XOq%oK:q%s/%q#g`_q#gldq#h/fq#h;kq#h`#q#CQ]q,\\bZnGiV4dXV<`RXkSbWWN@_dXV<BWBjb]WBt+hWC(IsWC1h)W5V^,")
(defn- cbk-code-b [] :string "~WBjb]WBt+hWC(IsWC1h)W5V^,eH7K)")
(defn- cbk-admit [M :vector-i64 i :i64] :bool
 (let [p (dec i) f (gn-sir M p IF-A)]
  (and (> p 0) (< (+ p 128) (vector-at M MM-SIR-N)) (= (gn-op M p) OP-FN) (> f 0) (< f (vector-at M MM-FN-N))
   (= (gn-fnf M f FF-SIR) p) (= (gn-fnf M f FF-NPARAMS) 2) (= (gn-fnf M f FF-PT0) TY-VEC)
   (= (gn-fnf M f (+ FF-PT0 1)) TY-I64) (= (gn-fnf M f FF-RTYPE) TY-VEC)
   (let [p8 (gn-sir M (+ p 42) IF-A) hs (gn-sir M (+ p 44) IF-A) bs (gn-sir M (+ p 64) IF-A) ex (gn-sir M (+ p 81) IF-A)
         s16 (gn-sir M (+ p 96) IF-A) pt (gn-sir M (+ p 97) IF-A) ac (gn-sir M (+ p 125) IF-A)
         hq (kfn-q M hs) bt (if (> hq 0) (gn-sir M (+ hq 4) IF-A) 0) hc (if (> hq 0) (gn-sir M (+ hq 12) IF-A) 0)
         eq (kfn-q M ex) pw (if (> eq 0) (gn-sir M (+ eq 15) IF-A) 0)]
    (and (> hq 0) (> eq 0) (> (kfn-q M ac) 0) (not= ac f) (not= hs f) (not= bs f) (not= ex f)
     (= (gn-fnf M ac FF-NPARAMS) 4) (= (gn-fnf M ac FF-PT0) TY-VEC) (= (gn-fnf M ac FF-RTYPE) TY-VEC)
     (= (gn-fnf M ac (+ FF-PT0 1)) TY-I64) (= (gn-fnf M ac (+ FF-PT0 2)) TY-I64) (= (gn-fnf M ac (+ FF-PT0 3)) TY-I64)
     (pj-fn? M f 128 (cbk-pat) [f p8 hs bs ex s16 pt ac 65535]) (pj-fn? M hs 15 (acs-pat) [hs bt hc])
     (pj-fn? M ex 36 (ace-pat) [ex pw s16]) (pj-fn? M s16 19 (pj-i16-pat) [s16 65535 32768 65536])
     (> (kfn-q M hc) 0) (> (kfn-q M bs) 0)
     (hfc-admit M (inc (kfn-q M hc))) (hbt-admit M (inc (kfn-q M bs)))
     (= (gn-sir M (+ (kfn-q M hc) 67) IF-A) bt) (= (gn-sir M (+ (kfn-q M bs) 86) IF-A) pw)
     (= (gn-sir M (+ (kfn-q M bs) 99) IF-A) pt) (= (gn-sir M (+ (kfn-q M bs) 72) IF-A) p8))))))
(defn- cbk-entry [M :vector-i64 i :i64] :vector-i64
 (if (not (cbk-admit M i)) M
  (let [ac (gn-sir M (+ (dec i) 125) IF-A)]
   (-> M (kemit-hex (cbk-code-a)) (gn-fix FX-BL26 ac) (gn-emit (enc-b 0)) (kemit-hex (cbk-code-b))))))
;; ---- picojpeg transformed-blocks: (f v count phase i): block = i rem 3, a = coefficient-block(v, block), rows =
;; idct-pass(a, false, 0), then (unless the last iteration with phase 1) cols = idct-pass(rows, true, 0), then (unless
;; the last with phase 2) rgb = color(cols, block, 0), then (unless the last) put16(rgb, 1413, rgb[1413] - 1) for
;; block 2 and the loop. Before the frame the whole loop runs here, coefficient-block called per iteration. After it,
;; when a is live with 2624 items, fuel covers the worst case of the rest (rows 281, columns 369, color 449, put16 2,
;; the loop 1) and the iteration is not a phase 1 / 2 exit, the two idct passes and color run fused in NEON, every
;; operation of the source performed: the rows pass as the idct-pass kernel computes it (eight lanes of i16, the lane
;; charges from the rows' nonzero masks), its output rows kept in registers as the columns pass's input (the rows
;; pass's 64 stores to v[1536 ..] are overwritten by the columns pass's, and the columns pass's reads of them are
;; served from those registers), the columns pass (lane-dc's charges from the i16 rows' zero masks, the DC fill
;; descale(s0) selected per column, multiply-idct as sqrdmulh by 128 f (plus the multiple of 256 of f), descale as
;; sqrshrun of the halved sum), its output bytes stored to v[1536 ..] as i64 and kept for color, which reads them
;; from there (c & 255 is c) and does its arithmetic per pixel on the low 16 bits of the planes' items (pixel-clamp
;; as sqxtun), eight pixels at a time, storing every put8. The charges are the source's, summed exactly; fuel never
;; runs short inside. Otherwise the iteration's rest is the calls themselves (vector-at with its own checks, the
;; loop's charge trapping as the source would). Generated and checked against the source semantics outside the
;; compiler (random and extreme blocks, all three color kinds). Carries the T2 keep marker after its ret. The SIRs of
;; transformed-blocks, rem, color, put8, put16, put, i16 and pixel-clamp are packed patterns; idct-pass passes the
;; idct-pass kernel's admission.
