;; ---- pb (kernels B): qrduino (place-byte v i j d limit) places data bits along the zigzag: while 8 i + j < limit,
;; at j = 8 the next byte d := v[i + 1] (one charge), else (d & 128: data-bit at the position v[1760], v[1761], two
;; charges), then next-free: advance (the zigzag state x y dy hv in v[1760 ..], stored & 255) until a module that is
;; not reserved (8 charges a step), d := 2 d & 255, j + 1, one charge. Non-leaf (slots in callee-saved registers, fuel
;; in memory). Fast path for v valid with |v| >= 1764: the state in registers, each bit's walk simulated first and
;; committed only when its charges fit and every position stays in [0, 24] (else the loop head takes that bit); the
;; final position is written back, the charges paid and the loop head goes on from i, j, d.
